+</svg><span class="pb-doclabel">Task guide</span></div>
+  <p class="pbv-eyebrow">Admin guideline · version 2</p>
+  <h1>Running Aurelia, <span class="pb-grad">one task at a time</span></h1>
+  <p class="pbv-lede">You don’t need to learn every screen. Find what you want to do, follow the steps, and mind the one thing to watch out for. Written for someone new to the team.</p>
+</header>
+
+<h2>New here? Start with these three things</h2>
+<div class="pbv-start">
+  <div><b>1. What the admin is</b><span>The team’s website for running Aurelia: people, the study, content, AI, money and privacy. It’s part of the same app people use, at <code>/admin</code>.</span></div>
+  <div><b>2. How to get in</b><span>Open <b>aureliaprod.vercel.app/admin</b> (production) or the staging site’s <code>/admin</code>. Enter the site password; ask the product owner, it is never written down.</span></div>
+  <div><b>3. Nothing is real yet</b><span>Every number is realistic sample data, and your edits only last for this visit. Explore freely, but never quote a figure as a result.</span></div>
+</div>
+<div class="pbv-believe pbv-soft"><b>Good to know:</b> there is no admin login yet, so anyone with the address and password can open it (the top known gap). Staging is the test copy where new things land first; production is what the client sees. Both have sample data.</div>
+
+<h2>Your first 15 minutes</h2>
+<ol class="pbv-three">
+  <li>Open <a href="/admin">the Dashboard</a> and click one card: every figure takes you to the page that owns it.</li>
+  <li>Open <a href="/admin/users">Users</a>, search for any name, and open that person.</li>
+  <li>Open <a href="/admin/moderation">Moderation</a> and sort by severity.</li>
+  <li>Open <a href="/admin/experimentation/v2">Feedback group · version 2</a> and look at the Milestones tab.</li>
+  <li>Skim the sidebar once. It’s grouped by job: Overview, People, Experimentation, Content, Intelligence, Revenue, Growth, Platform.</li>
+</ol>
+
+<h2>Who can do what</h2>
+<p>Five team roles. Give each person the smallest one that does their job. Roles take effect once admin login exists.</p>
+<table><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Can</th><th>Can’t</th></tr></thead><tbody>
+<tr><td><b>Super Admin</b></td><td>Everything, including roles and settings</td><td>Be reduced, so nobody can lock everyone out</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Operations</b></td><td>Day-to-day work on people and content; read AI monitoring</td><td>Change AI settings or roles, adjust coins</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Moderator</b></td><td>Review and act on reports</td><td>Edit people, AI or money</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>AI Engineer</b></td><td>Models, prompts, spend limits</td><td>Edit people or content</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Analyst</b></td><td>Read almost everything for reporting</td><td>Change anything</td></tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<p class="pbv-small">Full permission matrix: version 1 of this guide, “Roles and permissions”, or <a href="/admin/roles">Roles & permissions</a>.</p>
+
+<h2>Every morning (10 minutes)</h2>
+<div class="pbv-day">
+  <div><b>1 · Dashboard</b><span>“Needs attention”: what is waiting on someone. <a href="/admin">Open</a></span></div>
+  <div><b>2 · Moderation</b><span>Anything critical, and any self-harm or crisis report, first. <a href="/admin/moderation">Open</a></span></div>
+  <div><b>3 · Compliance</b><span>Any privacy request close to its deadline. <a href="/admin/compliance">Open</a></span></div>
+  <div><b>4 · AI monitoring</b><span>Errors or spend going up. <a href="/admin/ai">Open</a></span></div>
+  <div><b>5 · Study</b><span>If the study is running: This week. <a href="/admin/experimentation/v2">Open</a></span></div>
+</div>
+
+<h2>I want to…</h2>
+<p>Find your task, follow the steps. If it isn’t here, version 1 of this guide describes every screen in full.</p>
+<h3>People</h3>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Find someone</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/users">Users</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Type a name or email in the search box.</li><li>Use the filters (status, plan, role, country) to narrow it down.</li><li>Click the row to open their page.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>Always find people by search or id, never by guessing from a name.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">See one person’s history</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/users">Users → a person</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Open the person from Users.</li><li>Read their sessions, coins and the actions taken on their account.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>Their well-being panel is sample data today.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Change someone’s role, or suspend them</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/users">Users</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Find the person.</li><li>Pick a new role from the dropdown in their row, or press Suspend / Reactivate.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>It takes effect immediately. Only do it if your role allows it, and say why in your notes.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Invite a new team member</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/users">Users → Invite user</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Press Invite user.</li><li>Enter name, email and role, then Send invite.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>Give the smallest role that does the job (see “Who can do what”).</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Check whether people feel better</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/outcomes">Well-being outcomes</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Read the cards: who improved, the average change, who needs a follow-up.</li><li>Filter “follow-up” to see who scored 28 or less.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>A follow-up is for a person to make, never the app. A change here is not proof Aurelia caused it.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<h3>The feedback group study</h3>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Run the study day to day</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/experimentation/v2">Feedback group · version 2 → This week</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Open This week every morning.</li><li>Do the calls and follow-ups it lists, safety first.</li><li>Use the Milestones tab to see whether the next checkpoint is on track.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>The full routine is in the Feedback group playbook (version 2 is the easiest read).</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Write down a contact with a participant</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/experimentation/P01">A participant’s page → Coaching log</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Open the participant (P01–P30).</li><li>Add an entry: what they said, how they feel (1–5), the next step.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>Never write names or contact details. The log saves in your browser until the backend exists.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<h3>Content</h3>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Take a session off Explore</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/sessions">Sessions</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Find the session.</li><li>Press Unpublish in its row.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>It disappears from Explore and the community feed but stays in the author’s own library.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Create or change a challenge</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/challenges">Challenges</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Press New challenge, or Edit on a row.</li><li>Fill in title, summary, cover, days, minutes per day and points.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>Deleting asks you to confirm. The current design shows challenges without rankings.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Handle a report</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/moderation">Moderation</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Sort by severity: critical first.</li><li>Open the report and decide.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p><b>Self-harm or crisis reports go to the on-call reviewer straight away</b>, whatever their place in the queue.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<h3>AI</h3>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Check that the AI is healthy</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/ai">AI monitoring</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Look at the cards: error rate, slow requests (p95), refusals, quality score.</li><li>Check daily spend by model.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>A rising error rate or spend is red. Tell the AI engineer.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Change what the chat replies</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/cockpit-rules">Cockpit rules</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Find the rule whose trigger matches.</li><li>Edit its reply or the prompts it offers.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>Order matters: the first matching rule wins. This becomes “AI policies” when real AI arrives.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<h3>Money</h3>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">See how revenue is doing</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/revenue">Revenue</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Read monthly recurring revenue (MRR), churn and retention.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>All sample data; prices are not decided yet.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Find failed payments</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/payments">Payments → dunning queue</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Read the list of failed cards and their grace dates.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>No payment provider is connected yet.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Give or take coins</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/coins">Coins & rewards</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Find the entry in the ledger.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>Only with the coins.adjust permission. Every grant is written to the audit log.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<h3>Growth</h3>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Check an A/B test</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/experiments">Experiments (A/B)</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Find the test; read its lift and confidence.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>This is product testing, not the feedback-group study. A test that has run long without confidence should be stopped.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Check a message campaign</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/notifications">Notifications</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Read delivered, opened and converted for each campaign.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>Marketing messages need the person’s consent; payment or security messages do not.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<h3>Platform</h3>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Answer a privacy request (see or delete my data)</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/compliance">Compliance & privacy</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Open the request; check its due date and owner.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p><b>Overdue requests are a legal risk.</b> They come before anything else on this page.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Change what a wearable reads</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/signal-sources">Signal sources</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Edit the source’s name, group or what it reads.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>The “Reads” text is what people agreed to. Changing it means asking them again.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">See who changed what</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/audit">Audit log</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Search by person, action or date.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>The log can’t be edited or deleted.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><div><h4 class="pbv-task">Change a platform setting</h4><p class="pbv-when">Where: <a href="/admin/settings">Settings</a></p></div></div>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Steps</b><ol><li>Pick the AI model, set the monthly spend ceiling, or switch a feature on or off.</li></ol></div>
+    <div class="pbv-watch"><b>Watch out</b><p>These are written to the audit log. The demo’s own switches live elsewhere.</p></div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+
+<h2>Rules that always apply</h2>
+<div class="pbv-promises">
+  <div><b>Safety</b><ul><li>Anything about health or harm goes to a person, the same day. Nothing is acted on automatically.</li><li>Self-harm and crisis reports skip the queue.</li></ul></div>
+  <div><b>Care</b><ul><li>Deleting or removing always asks you to confirm. Read it.</li><li>Important changes are written to the audit log.</li><li>Changing consent text means asking people again.</li></ul></div>
+  <div><b>Honesty</b><ul><li>Sample data is never quoted as a result.</li><li>Overdue privacy requests are a legal risk, not a to-do.</li><li>Find people by id or search, never by guessing.</li></ul></div>
+</div>
+
+<h2>Words you’ll see</h2>
+<dl class="pbv-gloss">
+  <dt>Sample data</dt><dd>Realistic, generated numbers used until the backend exists.</dd>
+  <dt>Staging / production</dt><dd>The test copy of the site, and the real one the client sees.</dd>
+  <dt>WHO-5</dt><dd>A five-question well-being score from 0 to 100. +10 is a real change; 28 or less means a person follows up.</dd>
+  <dt>P01–P30</dt><dd>Code names for study participants. Real names never appear in the admin.</dd>
+  <dt>Coaching log</dt><dd>The project manager’s notes on each participant.</dd>
+  <dt>Cut / version</dt><dd>One built version of a session (v1.0, v1.1…).</dd>
+  <dt>MRR, churn</dt><dd>Monthly recurring revenue; the share of paying people who stop.</dd>
+  <dt>Dunning</dt><dd>Retrying a failed card payment before a subscription ends.</dd>
+  <dt>Privacy request (DSAR)</dt><dd>Someone asking to see, fix or delete their data. It has a legal deadline.</dd>
+  <dt>LLM-as-judge</dt><dd>An AI that scores a sample of the AI’s answers against a checklist.</dd>
+</dl>
+
+<h2>What’s coming</h2>
+<ul class="pbv-ticks">
+  <li><b>First:</b> real accounts, saved data, an admin login and the audit log.</li>
+  <li><b>Then:</b> AI monitoring and AI policies on real model calls.</li>
+  <li><b>Later:</b> payments, coins and challenges on real data, and every page on the database.</li>
+</ul>
+
+<div class="pbv-send">
+  <b>Start with the Dashboard, keep safety first, and ask before you change anything you can’t undo.</b>
+  <span>Every screen in full detail is in <b>version 1</b> of this guide.</span>
+</div>
+</div>
